      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SUNSET SESSION (3) landed the knockout blow last start when scoring his maiden victory over 1000m at Bunbury, storming home from the back. Out to 1200m now looks ideal and the barrier gives him the chance to sit closer in the run. Can bring up back-to-back wins. BOOKENDS (5) was trending the right way before tackling a Saturday race last time out and getting too far back to feature. She's back in grade today and the inside barrier should see her take much closer order. Pike sticking is a big push for her chances and she can return to winning ways. JUST WALTER JOHN (2) should find this much easier than what he's been tackling this campaign. He's third-up now and should be up front from the outset. There's enough there to suggest he can bounce back in a big way. FLASH DANCER (1) was too good last start at Northam and has to be included on the back of that effort. COSMIC WALTZ (6) missed by 1.2L fresh but that was a strong effort. Can raise the bar now.",
